retrieval_loop:
Sequence for a single query (unchanged gates, adopted from iteration 11; no new branch may depend on the census):
1. candidate scan over this patient's records with seq <= as_of_seq, hashed via the persistent store_meta index key;
2. gate 0 responsiveness test; candidates that share no real content term (or no digit-run/contact structural signal) are skipped;
3. rank survivors by (overlap_total desc, seq desc);
4. apply RBAC x relationship join and scope filter, producing allowed / denied_rbac / denied_scope;
5. tombstone check with tombstone_terms-scoped responsiveness -> denied_tombstone;
6. populate query_answer_denials as the count of RBAC/scope denials that share a real content term;
7. AFTER the above lists are final, append the candidate_census (a per-candidate, capped, read-nowhere list). Each entry carries the gate outcome for that candidate under the fixed status vocabulary allowed|deny_rbac|deny_scope|deny_tombstone|gate0_skip|unscanned. Nothing in this step branches action/answer/used_record_ids.
